# Test coverage is part of the change

Every PR that changes runtime behavior must add or update tests in the same PR.

- Map each changed decision branch, acceptance criterion, and named failure mode to a test.
- Test the happy path, rejection/error path, boundary values, and fallback/degraded behavior.
- Every bug fix includes a regression test that fails before the fix.
- Logic gets unit tests; process boundaries also get integration/contract tests.
- Assert observable outcomes and important side effects; do not write tests that only execute code.

Pure docs, comments, formatting, generated output, and non-behavioral config may omit tests only
when the PR body states `Test exemption:` and explains why runtime behavior cannot change.

Before commit/PR: list changed behaviors, confirm a test or valid exemption for each, then run
affected tests and all quality gates in `02-dev-workflow.mdc`. Existing tests passing is not enough.
